</table>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section class="ltx_appendix" id="A4" lang="en">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Analysis of Learning Dynamics</h2>
<div class="ltx_para" id="A4.p1">
<p class="ltx_p">This section provides a detailed visualization of the learning dynamics, complementing the analysis in the main body of the paper. Figure <a class="ltx_ref" href="https://arxiv.org/html/2509.09265v1#A4.F1" title="Figure D.1 ‣ Appendix D Analysis of Learning Dynamics ‣ Harnessing Uncertainty: Entropy-Modulated Policy Gradients for Long-Horizon LLM Agents"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a> illustrates the training progress of EMPG-enhanced agents compared to their baseline counterparts (GRPO and DAPO) on both the WebShop and ALFWorld benchmarks. As shown in the learning curves, the baseline agents consistently hit a performance ceiling, with their success rates stagnating early in the training process. In contrast, our EMPG-enhanced agents overcome this plateau, sustaining their learning momentum to achieve significantly higher final success rates across all settings. This evidence supports our central claim that EMPG provides a more effective learning signal, enabling agents to escape the local optima that trap standard policy gradient methods.</p>
</div>
<figure class="ltx_figure" id="A4.F1">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center" id="A4.F1.sf1"><img alt="Refer to caption" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" height="553" id="A4.F1.sf1.g1" src="x3.png" width="830"/>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><span class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">WebShop: GRPO</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</div>
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
